    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: slack-mcp-server 1.3.0

Model Context Protocol server for Slack (MIT). Exposes conversations, channel
and user directories, message history and search to MCP-capable clients over the
stdio and SSE transports. Authenticates with existing Slack session tokens or an
OAuth user token, so it needs no workspace app installation.

Go, vendored via the go_modules service. Upstream's &quot;-s -w&quot; link flags are not
used, so debuginfo is real. %check runs the suite with the TestIntegration cases
skipped -- they drive a live Slack workspace and an OpenAI endpoint and fail
rather than skip when credentials are absent; everything else passes.</comment>
